WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.832
Xie An was a famed scholar of the Eastern Jin; in his youth he lived in seclusion on East Mountain, leading a leisurely life.

00:00:06.182 --> 00:00:10.862
Every day he recited poetry and painted, roaming the hills and streams with his friends.

00:00:11.212 --> 00:00:16.780
When the country met with crisis, the court sent people again and again to ask him to come out and help.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:23.730
Xie An finally agreed; he put on his war robe and said farewell to his leisurely mountain life.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:29.240
Below the mountain, the people lined the road to welcome him, full of hope in him.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:35.278
He calmly arranged the battle plans — devising strategies in the tent that would decide victory a thousand li away.

00:00:35.628 --> 00:00:40.188
After hearing his plan, the generals and soldiers all felt their hearts settle.

00:00:40.538 --> 00:00:46.370
The Eastern Jin army crushed the Former Qin at the Fei River, and Xie An's contribution could not be overlooked.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:54.208
From then on, 'rising again from East Mountain' has been used to describe rallying after a fall and creating new glory.

00:00:54.558 --> 00:00:59.070
As long as we do not give up, everyone has a chance to rise again from East Mountain.

